Title: Add com Jenkins agent AMI to monthly cadence

First, I investigated the existing automation to understand how the Jenkins agent AMI was being created. I found that we already had an Ansible playbook responsible for creating the Jenkins agent AMI, including applying the required OS updates and patches.

My requirement was to make sure Terraform used the appropriate monthly Jenkins agent AMI. So I modified the Ansible automation to add a cadence=monthly tag to the AMI when it was created.

Then, on the Terraform side, I used the aws_ami data source to query AWS for the Jenkins agent AMI. I added filters for the Jenkins agent role and the monthly cadence, and used most_recent = true so Terraform would select the latest matching AMI.

The AMI ID returned by the data source was then referenced using data.aws_ami.jenkins_agent.id in the Jenkins agent infrastructure configuration. This allowed the Jenkins agent infrastructure to use the latest monthly patched AMI rather than relying on a manually hardcoded AMI ID.

Since I didn't have permission to manage Jenkins or run Terraform directly against the environment, I made the code changes and raised them through the team's PR/CI process, where the authorized team could run the Terraform plan and apply.

             ANSIBLE
                │
                ▼
     Create Jenkins Agent AMI
                │
       Apply OS patches
                │
                ▼
         Add tag:
       cadence = monthly
                │
                ▼
          AWS AMI
         ami-12345
                │
                │
                ▼
            TERRAFORM
                │
       aws_ami data source
                │
                ▼
      Find matching AMIs
                │
       most_recent = true
                │
                ▼
data.aws_ami.jenkins_agent.id
                │
                ▼
    Jenkins Agent infrastructure
                │
                ▼
        New Jenkins Agent
1. Terraform (replace hardcoded AMI usage)
# Fetch the latest monthly Jenkins Agent AMI
data "aws_ami" "jenkins_agent" {
  owners      = ["self"]   # replace with your AWS Account ID if needed
  most_recent = true

  filter {
    name   = "tag:role"
    values = ["jenkins-agent"]
  }

  filter {
    name   = "tag:cadence"
    values = ["monthly"]
  }
}

# Example Launch Template using the AMI
resource "aws_launch_template" "jenkins_agent" {
  name          = "jenkins-agent-template"
  image_id      = data.aws_ami.jenkins_agent.id
  instance_type = "t3.medium" # adjust if needed

  # Keep existing settings like IAM role, SGs, user_data etc.
  # user_data = file("jenkins_agent_userdata.sh")
  # iam_instance_profile { name = "jenkins-agent-profile" }
}

2. Ansible (add AMI tagging during bake)
- name: Create Jenkins Agent AMI
  amazon.aws.ec2_ami:
    instance_id: "{{ ec2_id }}"
    name: "jenkins-agent-{{ lookup('pipe','date +%Y%m') }}"
    region: us-east-1
    wait: yes
    tags:
      role: jenkins-agent
      cadence: monthly
      created_by: ansible
